      <main id="wfLandingMain" class="wf-landing__main">
        <section class="wf-landing-hero dw-card">
          <p class="wf-landing-hero__eyebrow">Classroom writing tool</p>
          <h1 class="dw-h1">Timed writing that meets every learner where they are.</h1>
          <p class="dw-lead">WriteFlow Studio lets teachers build assignments with custom prompts, timers, vocabulary goals, and accessibility options. Students get a focused writing screen — no clutter, no paste, just type.</p>
          <div class="wf-landing-hero__cta">
            <a class="dw-btn wf-landing-cta" href="/writeflow/studio/">Open WriteFlow Studio</a>
            <a class="dw-btn dw-btn-ghost" href="/writeflow/setup/">Google Sheets setup</a>
          </div>
          <p class="dw-muted dw-tiny">Student assignment links look like <code>/writeflow/a/?id=your-assignment</code> — share only those with students.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="wf-landing-stats dw-card" aria-labelledby="wfStatsTitle">
          <h2 class="dw-h2" id="wfStatsTitle">Impact so far</h2>
          <p class="wf-landing-stat">
            <span class="wf-landing-stat__value" id="wfSentenceCount">—</span>
            <span class="wf-landing-stat__label">sentences analyzed by WriteFlow</span>
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="wf-landing-welcome dw-card">
          <h2 class="dw-h2">What is WriteFlow?</h2>
          <div class="wf-landing-columns">
            <div>
              <h3 class="dw-h3">For teachers</h3>
              <p class="dw-muted">Build assignments in WriteFlow Studio — set prompts, time limits, minimum word counts, expected vocabulary, and class codes. Save and publish to get a student link. Open Results to review submissions, highlight vocabulary usage, and export CSV.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="dw-h3">For students</h3>
              <p class="dw-muted">Students open only their assignment link. They see the prompt, a timer, live word count and WPM, and a typing area. Pasting is blocked by default. When time is up (or they finish early), WriteFlow analyzes typing stamina, mechanics, and content.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="wf-landing-tutorial dw-card" aria-labelledby="wfTutorialTitle">
          <h2 class="dw-h2" id="wfTutorialTitle">Quick tutorial</h2>
